"Morning light slipped through the dusty panes of Elias Harrow’s workshop, catching the brass gears that lay like sleeping insects on his bench. He lifted the unfinished timepiece, its wooden case polished to a honeyed glow, and set the tiny escapement into place. The mechanism was unlike any he had crafted before; each tick lingered a heartbeat longer than the last, slipping a fraction behind the world’s relentless march. He smiled, feeling the subtle rebellion of the gears, and whispered a promise to the silent seconds that would soon betray their usual haste. Outside, the town’s bells rang on schedule, oblivious to the quiet conspiracy hidden within his creation."

